# This repository is LF everywhere, and must stay LF in a Windows checkout.
#
# docs/example-maturity-report.html and docs/example-badge.json are published
# artefacts that tests/test_pilot_example.py compares byte for byte against a
# fresh `pumllint score` run. Git for Windows checks text files out as CRLF by
# default, so without this the committed copies and the freshly generated ones
# differ on every line — a failure with nothing to do with the tool.
* text=auto eol=lf
